# Names are scoped by shape, and a reference or a patch spells every shape on the way down. 192x64,
# three cells on paper at 64px pitch, each one `bug` instance centered at y 32. A bug is a blue
# circle `thorax` (radius 14) on the left of its cell and a green circle `abdomen` (radius 10) on
# the right. Each body circle holds a small gold circle named `sheen` in its upper left, the
# abdomen's inside a `group gloss`, so the same short name is declared twice, once under each shape.
# 1. Cell 1 (x 32): the bug as declared. A gold sheen on the thorax and a gold sheen on the abdomen.
# 2. Cell 2 (x 96): `.abdomen.sheen fill:p.red` turns only the abdomen's sheen red. The thorax's
# sheen stays gold.
# 3. Cell 3 (x 160): `.thorax.sheen off` removes the thorax's sheen, so the blue circle is plain. A
# red ring (radius 6, no fill) placed at `@b3.abdomen.sheen.cx,@b3.abdomen.sheen.cy` is centered
# on the abdomen's gold sheen, which stays gold. The group around that sheen is not part of the
# path.
@target structure/shape_scope.png 192x64

def bug
  circle 14 at:-14,4 fill:p.blue name:thorax
    circle 4 at:-5,-6 fill:p.gold name:sheen
  circle 10 at:14,0 fill:p.green name:abdomen
    group gloss
      circle 3 at:-3,-4 fill:p.gold name:sheen

bug at:32,32 name:b1

bug at:96,32 name:b2
  .abdomen.sheen fill:p.red

bug at:160,32 name:b3
  .thorax.sheen off

circle 6 at:@b3.abdomen.sheen.cx,@b3.abdomen.sheen.cy fill:none stroke:p.red,1.5
